Provenance and licensing notice
================================

This repository (BonDriver_Userland) contains newly written C++17 source,
build files and tests for shared libraries that drive the siano-userland and
px4-userland command line tools. It does not bundle any third-party source
files or headers. Compiler-runtime license texts are included under licenses/.

ABI compatibility and adapters
------------------------------
The public interface and the EDCB structure layouts in
include/bondriver/Abi.h exist so that existing BonDriver consumers (EDCB and
LibISDB) can load these libraries. Vtable order and structure layout are
functional compatibility requirements; equivalent declarations are also used
independently by consumers. The C-structure adapter functions that fill and
forward the structure slots are implemented in this project
(src/common/DriverCore.cpp); the EDCB inline adapter bodies are not copied.

The optional test tests/edcb_compile_check.cpp compiles against an EDCB
checkout supplied by the operator at configure time. EDCB and LibISDB are not
redistributed here.

Consulted references (read only)
--------------------------------
- EDCB BonDriver interface declarations (BonCtrl/IBonDriver.h, IBonDriver2.h)
  were inspected to validate the ABI: https://github.com/Khronos31/EDCB
- LibISDB BonDriver interface declarations
  (LibISDB/Windows/Base/BonDriver.hpp) were inspected to validate the ABI and
  to confirm that consumers use the pointer form of GetTsStream.
- BonDriver reference implementations in the Khronos31/hassio-addons EDCB
  add-on (https://github.com/Khronos31/hassio-addons) and in
  Khronos31/Pochitto (https://github.com/Khronos31/Pochitto) were consulted
  for tuning and behavioral knowledge; their code is not included.
- Child CLI contracts (option names, units, channel frequency formulas) are
  taken from the siano-userland (https://github.com/Khronos31/siano-userland)
  and px4-userland (https://github.com/Khronos31/px4-userland) documentation.

